# Project Documentation

This page is the single documentation entry point. Replace every route below
with local files that exist in the target repository.

## Start Here

For engineering work:

1. Read the source requirement or issue.
2. Read the approved design and acceptance document, if they exist.
3. Read relevant Knowledge Base maps.
4. Apply the relevant Skill.
5. Inspect current code and tests.
6. Follow `CONTRIBUTING.md`.

## Documentation Map

| Question | Local canonical location |
| --- | --- |
| Product requirements and roadmap | `[path]` |
| Current technical behavior | `docs/knowledge/README.md` |
| Reusable engineering procedures | `docs/skills/README.md` |
| Architecture decisions | `[design document convention]` |
| Manual acceptance | `[acceptance document convention]` |
| Delivery workflow | `CONTRIBUTING.md` |
| Deferred risks | `PRODUCTION_READINESS_BACKLOG.md` |
| Release history | `[release notes path]` |

## Documentation Lifecycle

- Knowledge Base maps change with shipped behavior and tests.
- Design documents change with decisions and delivery status.
- Skills change only after a reusable procedure is demonstrated.
- Acceptance documents record only executed manual evidence.
- Live project status changes at milestone closeout; historical snapshots stay
  historical.
